                <pb facs="0534" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4028: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Ceiba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Evans</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ceiba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-14T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 14,
                                1926—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s telegram of November 10, 6 p.m., received November 13,
                    9 a.m. The Governor published his statement in the only newspaper appearing last
                    evening and informs me that publication will be made in all the local press. He
                    states that the military authorities proceeded yesterday to take steps to
                    inflict disciplinary punishment upon the <hi rendition="#italic">mayor de
                        plaza</hi> who will cease to exercise his functions on November 15th. Will
                    report further by cable. Repeated to Legation at Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Evans</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
